## When stuck

1. Read the error message fully. `platform check` prints what failed, where, and how to fix it.
2. Reproduce locally: run the tests, run the app with `{{DEV_COMMAND}}`, call `/healthz`, `/readyz`.
3. For a failed pipeline run or a broken environment, ask the user to open the app in the portal
   ({{APP_PORTAL_URL}}) and paste the "copy prompt for your AI agent" text or the relevant log
   lines (portal log viewer, "copy prompt for AI").
4. Load `troubleshooting`; it maps common symptoms (crash loop, 401/403, 502/503, database
   sign-in errors, missing env var) to causes.
5. If the cause is on the platform side (permissions, network, a resource that doesn't exist yet,
   approval), say so plainly and suggest the user contacts the platform team through the portal.
   Don't work around platform controls.

